course: dictionary
lesson: 10162
title: Days of the week
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Thursday is a day of the week. It comes after Wednesday and before Friday. A week has 7 days, and Thursday is one of them.
explain: You can find Thursday by counting. Start on Tuesday and count two days on: Wednesday, then Thursday. «The day after the day after Tuesday is Thursday.» Counting forward and back helps you with dates and timetables.
explain: The word can also show repeat. «On Thursdays» means every Thursday, not just one day. «See you on Thursday» means on the Thursday that is coming next.
fact: Thursday is a noun, and its plural is Thursdays.
fact: Thursday is the day after Wednesday and before Friday.
fact: «On Thursdays» means every Thursday.
fact: Thursday is named after Thor, the Norse god of thunder.
fact: In French, Thursday is «jeudi».
exercise: What day comes after Wednesday? | Sunday | *Thursday | Tuesday
exercise: Today is Tuesday. What day is it two days later? | *Thursday | Monday | Friday | Wednesday
exercise: «On Thursdays» means what? | Thursday afternoons only | *Every Thursday | Only one Thursday in the year | Thursday in the summer
test: «Halloween, 31 October 2026, is a Saturday, and Bonfire Night, 5 November, is 5 days later.» What day is Bonfire Night? | Wednesday | Sunday | *Thursday
test: What is «jeudi» in English? | *Thursday | Friday | Wednesday | Tuesday
exam: Mr Hughes has a cold on Monday and is really ill on Tuesday. He is in hospital on Wednesday. On which day does he walk in with a cup of tea? | Monday | Friday | *Thursday | Tuesday
